{
  "tickets": [
    {
      "id": "gen-151",
      "subject": "Inquiry Regarding Missing Personal Medication Preference Lists",
      "body": "Dear Support Team, I am writing to inquire about my personal medication favorites list, which appears to have disappeared following the recent software update. Saving frequently prescribed drugs and sigs is essential for my daily workflow efficiency here at the clinic. Could you please advise on how we might restore these custom settings? Thank you for your assistance.",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-152",
      "subject": "Sorry to bother, question on handling out-of-stock pharmacy alerts",
      "body": "Hello, I am so sorry to bother you with this, but I am having some trouble figuring out the best way to handle out-of-stock medication alerts and switching a patient over to an alternative therapeutic agent. I keep getting pharmacy substitution messages and honestly I am not entirely sure I am clicking through the right workflow. Could you please point me in the right direction when you have a moment? Apologies again for taking up your time.",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-153",
      "subject": "How to send lab results to covering doctors?",
      "body": "Hello, I am trying to figure out how to route abnormal lab results over to our covering physicians before filing them in the chart. Can you please send instructions?",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-154",
      "subject": "Pharmacy directory search and custom entry",
      "body": "We need to update a patient's preferred pharmacy since their usual location closed down. How do we search the integrated directory for the new branch and add a custom entry if it fails to appear? Please advise.",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-155",
      "subject": "Confused about routing abnormal labs to covering physicians",
      "body": "Hi there, I am a bit turned around regarding the lab review workflow. I know I need to sign off and annotate incoming lab results, but I am struggling to find where I can route abnormal results to my covering physician while I am away next week. Could you clarify how this is supposed to be done?",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-156",
      "subject": "Trouble attaching outside paper lab PDFs to patient charts",
      "body": "Hello, I am quite confused about how to properly upload and attach external paper lab reports and outside imaging PDFs into patient charts. I tried scanning a multi-page lab report this morning and went to the documents tab, clicked upload, and selected the file from my desktop, but the system kept giving me a generic format error and refusing to accept the file size. I tried compressing the PDF and splitting it into smaller chunks, but I keep getting stuck at the preview screen. Could you please walk me through the correct file format requirements and steps to get these outside reports attached successfully?",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-157",
      "subject": "Updating provider schedule working hours",
      "body": "Hello, could you please help us adjust the weekly availability and calendar blocks for one of our providers whose working hours are currently displaying incorrectly?",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-158",
      "subject": "Questions on setting up user roles and permission levels",
      "body": "Hello, I am looking at the user management settings and I am feeling a bit confused about how to create custom security roles. I want to restrict access to certain financial and clinical records for our newer staff members, but the permission level toggles are not entirely clear to me. Could someone guide me through how to properly configure these roles without locking everyone out?",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-159",
      "subject": "Frustrated with compliance archive settings and data backup configuration",
      "body": "I have spent the better part of the morning trying to figure out where we are supposed to configure our data backup schedules and establish our compliance archive settings. I went into the administration panel, looked under settings, and checked security, but nothing matches what is described in the manual. Every time I try to run a historical data export for our compliance audit, the system throws an unhelpful error code instead of generating the report. This is extremely frustrating because we need these backups squared away immediately; please have someone call me or give me clear instructions on how to fix this right away.",
      "id_alt": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-160",
      "subject": "Apologies, urgent help needed with EPCS token failure and incorrect prescription transmission",
      "body": "Hello support, I am so sorry to reach out about this urgently, but we have a major issue with a controlled substance prescription that went completely wrong today. While trying to complete my two-factor authentication token signing for EPCS, my token failed right in the middle of transmission, and somehow an incorrect medication dosage was sent out to the patient's pharmacy for a controlled substance. I tried to cancel it through the outbound queue, but the status is currently stuck in limbo and I am worried about patient safety. Could you please forgive the panic, look into this transmission failure immediately, and help me retract and correct this prescription right away?",
      "id_alt": null
    }
  ]
}
